<title>INDIA: India approves $25 mln Cargill flour investment.</title>
<headline>India approves $25 mln Cargill flour investment.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian Industry Ministry said on Friday that it approved a $25 million capital investment by Cargill Asia Pacific Ltd to permit its Indian subsidiary to enter into the flour milling business.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the investment was expected to lead to 1.67 billion rupees' worth of exports over four years.</p>
</text>
